-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1, sections 109, 110, 112 and 113 (piece dg1): bylaws, emergency
-- bylaws and emergency powers, access to proxy solicitation materials, and proxy expense reimbursement.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively; nobody's point of view.
--
-- Source: de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt, a plain-text rendering of the Delaware Code Online, not the
-- official text. `-- src:N | ...` is a slice of line N; an ellipsis means the line goes on.
--
-- Section 114(a) reads "stockholders" as "members" (and "board of directors" as "governing body") for a nonstock
-- corporation, except in the places section 114(b) and (c) list (section 109(a) and the last sentence of 109(b)
-- among them). This module is written, as section 109(a) is, out of the words of the text: the nonstock reading is
-- made in each rule that mentions the kind of corporation; the reading as a whole is in dg1-s114-nonstock.l4.

§ `Section 109 -- Bylaws`

§§ `s 109(a) Who holds the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws`

-- src:141 | (a) The original or other bylaws of a corporation may be adopted, amended or repealed by the incorporators, by the initial directors of a corporation other than a nonstock corporation or initial members of the governing body of a nonstock corporation if they were named in the certificate of incorporation, or, before a corporation other than a nonstock corporation has received any payment for any of its stock, by its board of directors. …
-- src:141 | After a corporation other than a nonstock corporation has received any payment for any of its stock, the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws shall be in the stockholders entitled to vote. In the case of a nonstock corporation, the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws shall be in its members entitled to …
-- src:141 | In the case of a nonstock corporation, the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws shall be in its members entitled to vote. …
-- src:141 | Notwithstanding the foregoing, any corporation may, in its certificate of incorporation, confer the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws upon the directors or, in the case of a nonstock corporation, upon its governing body. …
-- src:141 | The fact that such power has been so conferred upon the directors or governing body, as the case may be, shall not divest the stockholders or members of the power, nor limit their power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 109(a) (src:141)
DECLARE `s 109(a) Holder of the power over the bylaws` IS ONE OF
    `the incorporators as holders of the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws`
    `the initial directors of a corporation other than a nonstock corporation, if named in the certificate of incorporation`
    `the initial members of the governing body of a nonstock corporation, if named in the certificate of incorporation`
    `the board of directors of a corporation other than a nonstock corporation, before the corporation has received any payment for any of its stock`
    `the stockholders entitled to vote, after a corporation other than a nonstock corporation has received any payment for any of its stock`
    `the members of a nonstock corporation entitled to vote`
    `the directors or, in the case of a nonstock corporation, the governing body, on whom the certificate of incorporation confers the power`

-- The original or other bylaws may be adopted, amended or repealed by the incorporators; by the initial directors of
-- a corporation other than a nonstock corporation, or the initial members of the governing body of a nonstock
-- corporation, if they were named in the certificate; or, before a corporation other than a nonstock corporation has
-- received any payment for any of its stock, by its board. After that payment the power is in the stockholders
-- entitled to vote. In a nonstock corporation it is in its members entitled to vote. Any corporation may, in its
-- certificate, confer the power on the directors (or governing body); that does not divest the stockholders or
-- members of the power, nor limit it. Reading taken (Fork register): "the power ... shall be in the stockholders
-- entitled to vote" is exclusive, so for a corporation other than a nonstock corporation the power of the
-- incorporators, of the initial directors and of the board ends at the first payment for any of its stock; for a
-- nonstock corporation the text names no event that ends the incorporators' or the initial members' power, so the
-- rule does not end it.
-- src:141 | (a) The original or other bylaws of a corporation may be adopted, amended or repealed by the incorporators, by the initial directors of a corporation other than a nonstock corporation or initial members of the governing body of a nonstock corporation if they were named in the certificate of incorporation, or, before a corporation other than a nonstock corporation has received any payment for any of its stock, by its board of directors. …
-- src:141 | After a corporation other than a nonstock corporation has received any payment for any of its stock, the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws shall be in the stockholders entitled to vote. In the case of a nonstock corporation, the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws shall be in its members entitled to …
-- src:141 | In the case of a nonstock corporation, the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws shall be in its members entitled to vote. …
-- src:141 | Notwithstanding the foregoing, any corporation may, in its certificate of incorporation, confer the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws upon the directors or, in the case of a nonstock corporation, upon its governing body. …
-- src:141 | The fact that such power has been so conferred upon the directors or governing body, as the case may be, shall not divest the stockholders or members of the power, nor limit their power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 109(a) (src:141)
GIVEN holder IS A `s 109(a) Holder of the power over the bylaws`
      kind IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the initial directors, or the initial members of the governing body, were named in the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation has received any payment for any of its stock` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation confers the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws upon the directors or governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 109(a) the holder has the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws` holder kind `the initial directors, or the initial members of the governing body, were named in the certificate of incorporation` `the corporation has received any payment for any of its stock` `the certificate of incorporation confers the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws upon the directors or governing body` MEANS
    CONSIDER holder
    WHEN `the incorporators as holders of the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws` THEN
        (`the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind) OR (NOT (`the corporation has received any payment for any of its stock`))
    WHEN `the initial directors of a corporation other than a nonstock corporation, if named in the certificate of incorporation` THEN
            (NOT (`the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind))
        AND `the initial directors, or the initial members of the governing body, were named in the certificate of incorporation`
        AND (NOT (`the corporation has received any payment for any of its stock`))
    WHEN `the initial members of the governing body of a nonstock corporation, if named in the certificate of incorporation` THEN
            (`the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind)
        AND `the initial directors, or the initial members of the governing body, were named in the certificate of incorporation`
    WHEN `the board of directors of a corporation other than a nonstock corporation, before the corporation has received any payment for any of its stock` THEN
            (NOT (`the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind))
        AND (NOT (`the corporation has received any payment for any of its stock`))
    WHEN `the stockholders entitled to vote, after a corporation other than a nonstock corporation has received any payment for any of its stock` THEN
            (NOT (`the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind))
        AND `the corporation has received any payment for any of its stock`
    WHEN `the members of a nonstock corporation entitled to vote` THEN
        `the kind is a nonstock corporation` kind
    WHEN `the directors or, in the case of a nonstock corporation, the governing body, on whom the certificate of incorporation confers the power` THEN
        `the certificate of incorporation confers the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws upon the directors or governing body`

-- "The fact that such power has been so conferred upon the directors or governing body shall not divest the
-- stockholders or members of the power, nor limit their power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws."
-- src:141 | The fact that such power has been so conferred upon the directors or governing body, as the case may be, shall not divest the stockholders or members of the power, nor limit their power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 109(a) (src:141)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation confers the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws upon the directors or governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 109(a) the conferral of the power on the directors or governing body divests the stockholders or members of the power` `the certificate of incorporation confers the power to adopt, amend or repeal bylaws upon the directors or governing body` MEANS FALSE

§§ `s 109(b) What the bylaws may contain`

-- src:142 | (b) The bylaws may contain any provision, not inconsistent with law or with the certificate of incorporation, relating to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, and its rights or powers or the rights or powers of its stockholders, directors, officers or employees. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 109(b) (src:142)
GIVEN `the provision relates to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or its rights or powers or the rights or powers of its stockholders, directors, officers or employees` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is inconsistent with law or with the certificate of incorporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 109(b) the bylaws may contain the provision` `the provision relates to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or its rights or powers or the rights or powers of its stockholders, directors, officers or employees` `the provision is inconsistent with law or with the certificate of incorporation` MEANS
        `the provision relates to the business of the corporation, the conduct of its affairs, or its rights or powers or the rights or powers of its stockholders, directors, officers or employees`
    AND (NOT (`the provision is inconsistent with law or with the certificate of incorporation`))

-- The bylaws may not contain a provision that would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees or
-- expenses of the corporation or any other party in connection with an internal corporate claim, as defined in
-- section 115 (dg1-s111-s115-jurisdiction-and-forum.l4), or in connection with any other claim that a stockholder,
-- acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or
-- proceeding.
-- src:142 | The bylaws may not contain any provision that would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys’ fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party in connection with an internal corporate claim, as defined in § 115 of this title, or in connection with any other claim that a stockholder, acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 109(b) (src:142)
GIVEN `the provision would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is one that a stockholder, acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 109(b) the bylaws may contain the provision on fees and expenses` `the provision would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party` `the claim is based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity` `this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim` `the claim is one that a stockholder, acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or proceeding` MEANS
    NOT (    `the provision would impose liability on a stockholder for the attorneys' fees or expenses of the corporation or any other party`
         AND (   `s 115(b) the claim is an internal corporate claim` `the claim is based upon a violation of a duty by a current or former director or officer or stockholder in such capacity` `this title confers jurisdiction upon the Court of Chancery as to the claim`
              OR `the claim is one that a stockholder, acting in its capacity as a stockholder or in the right of the corporation, has brought in an action, suit or proceeding`))

§ `Section 110 -- Emergency bylaws and other powers in emergency`

§§ `s 110(a) Emergency bylaws`

-- src:146 | (a) The board of directors of any corporation may adopt emergency bylaws, subject to repeal or change by action of the stockholders, which, notwithstanding any different provision elsewhere in this chapter or in Chapters 3 [repealed] and 5 [repealed] of Title 26, or in Chapter 7 of Title 5, or in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, shall be operative during any emergency resulting from an attack on the United States or on a locality in which the corporation conducts its business or customarily holds meetings of its board of directors or its stockholders, or during any nuclear or atomic disaster, or during the existence of any catastrophe, including, but not limited to, an epidemic or pandemic, and a declaration of a national emergency by the United States government, or other similar emergency condition, irrespective …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(a) (src:146)
DECLARE `s 110(a) Emergency` IS ONE OF
    `an attack on the United States or on a locality in which the corporation conducts its business or customarily holds meetings of its board of directors or its stockholders`
    `a nuclear or atomic disaster`
    `the existence of a catastrophe, including, but not limited to, an epidemic or pandemic, and a declaration of a national emergency by the United States government`
    `another similar emergency condition`
    `no emergency`

-- The board may adopt emergency bylaws, subject to repeal or change by action of the stockholders, operative during
-- any emergency of the kinds listed, irrespective of whether a quorum of the board or a standing committee can readily
-- be convened, and notwithstanding any different provision elsewhere in the chapter, in Chapters 3 and 5 of Title 26
-- or Chapter 7 of Title 5 (Titles 26 and 5: no input needed, the text itself overrides them), or in the certificate or
-- bylaws. Upon the termination of the emergency they cease to be operative (subsection (e)).
-- src:146 | (a) The board of directors of any corporation may adopt emergency bylaws, subject to repeal or change by action of the stockholders, which, notwithstanding any different provision elsewhere in this chapter or in Chapters 3 [repealed] and 5 [repealed] of Title 26, or in Chapter 7 of Title 5, or in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, shall be operative during any emergency resulting from an attack on the United States or on a locality in which the corporation conducts its business or customarily holds meetings of its board of directors or its stockholders, or during any nuclear or atomic disaster, or during the existence of any catastrophe, including, but not limited to, an epidemic or pandemic, and a declaration of a national emergency by the United States government, or other similar emergency condition, irrespective of whether a quorum of the board of directors or a standing committee thereof can readily be convened for action. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(a) (src:146)
GIVEN emergency IS A `s 110(a) Emergency`
      `emergency bylaws have been adopted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the emergency has terminated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(a) the emergency bylaws are operative` emergency `emergency bylaws have been adopted` `the emergency has terminated` MEANS
        `emergency bylaws have been adopted`
    AND (NOT (emergency EQUALS `no emergency`))
    AND (NOT (`the emergency has terminated`))

-- src:153 | (e) To the extent not inconsistent with any emergency bylaws so adopted, the bylaws of the corporation shall remain in effect during any emergency and upon its termination the emergency bylaws shall cease to be operative.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(e) (src:153)
GIVEN `the bylaw is inconsistent with the emergency bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(e) the bylaw of the corporation remains in effect during the emergency` `the bylaw is inconsistent with the emergency bylaws` MEANS
    NOT (`the bylaw is inconsistent with the emergency bylaws`)

-- Adoption: by the board of directors or, if a quorum cannot be readily convened for a meeting, by a majority of the
-- directors present. The text does not define a "majority of the directors present" at a meeting without a quorum, so
-- it is counted against the directors present (more than half of them).
-- src:146 | irrespective of whether a quorum of the board of directors or a standing committee thereof can readily be convened for action. The emergency bylaws contemplated by this section may be adopted by the board of directors or, if a quorum cannot be readily convened for a meeting, by a majority of the directors present. The emergency bylaws …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(a) (src:146)
GIVEN `a quorum of the board of directors can readily be convened for a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board of directors adopted the emergency bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of the directors present who voted to adopt them` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of the directors present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(a) the emergency bylaws were validly adopted` `a quorum of the board of directors can readily be convened for a meeting` `the board of directors adopted the emergency bylaws` `the number of the directors present who voted to adopt them` `the number of the directors present` MEANS
    IF `a quorum of the board of directors can readily be convened for a meeting`
    THEN JUST `the board of directors adopted the emergency bylaws`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the vote carries` (`a majority of` (`another base named in the provision` "the directors present")) `the number of the directors present who voted to adopt them` `the number of the directors present`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST byMajority THEN JUST (`the board of directors adopted the emergency bylaws` OR byMajority)

-- src:146 | (a) The board of directors of any corporation may adopt emergency bylaws, subject to repeal or change by action of …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(a) (src:146)
GIVEN `the emergency bylaws were adopted by the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(a) the emergency bylaws are subject to repeal or change by action of the stockholders` `the emergency bylaws were adopted by the board of directors` MEANS
    `the emergency bylaws were adopted by the board of directors`

-- The emergency bylaws may make any provision that may be practical and necessary for the circumstances of the
-- emergency, including three the text lists.
-- src:146 | The emergency bylaws may make any provision that may be practical and necessary for the circumstances of the emergency, including provisions that:
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(a) (src:146)
GIVEN `the provision is practical and necessary for the circumstances of the emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(a) the emergency bylaws may make the provision` `the provision is practical and necessary for the circumstances of the emergency` MEANS
    `the provision is practical and necessary for the circumstances of the emergency`

-- src:147 | (1) A meeting of the board of directors or a committee thereof may be called by any officer or director in such manner and under such conditions as shall be prescribed in the emergency bylaws;
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(a)(1) (src:147)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the call is made in the manner and under the conditions prescribed in the emergency bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(a)(1) the person may call a meeting of the board of directors or a committee` `the person is an officer or a director` `the call is made in the manner and under the conditions prescribed in the emergency bylaws` MEANS
        `the person is an officer or a director`
    AND `the call is made in the manner and under the conditions prescribed in the emergency bylaws`

-- The director or directors in attendance, or any greater number fixed by the emergency bylaws, constitute a quorum.
-- src:148 | (2) The director or directors in attendance at the meeting, or any greater number fixed by the emergency bylaws, shall constitute a quorum; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(a)(2) (src:148)
GIVEN `the number of directors in attendance at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the greater number fixed by the emergency bylaws` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(a)(2) the directors in attendance constitute a quorum` `the number of directors in attendance at the meeting` `the greater number fixed by the emergency bylaws` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the greater number fixed by the emergency bylaws`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the number of directors in attendance at the meeting` AT LEAST 1
    WHEN JUST fixed THEN `the number of directors in attendance at the meeting` AT LEAST fixed

-- The officers or other persons designated on a list approved by the board before the emergency, in the order of
-- priority, on the conditions and for the period provided, not longer than reasonably necessary after the
-- emergency ends, are, to the extent required to provide a quorum, deemed directors for the meeting.
-- src:149 | (3) The officers or other persons designated on a list approved by the board of directors before the emergency, all in such order of priority and subject to such conditions and for such period of time (not longer than reasonably necessary after the termination of the emergency) as may be provided in the emergency bylaws or in the resolution approving the list, shall, to the extent required to provide a quorum at any meeting of the board of directors, be deemed directors for such meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(a)(3) (src:149)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or other person designated on a list approved by the board of directors before the emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's turn in the order of priority has come and the conditions provided in the emergency bylaws or the resolution approving the list are met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of time has not run beyond what is reasonably necessary after the termination of the emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deeming is required to provide a quorum at the meeting of the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(a)(3) the person is deemed a director for the meeting` `the person is an officer or other person designated on a list approved by the board of directors before the emergency` `the person's turn in the order of priority has come and the conditions provided in the emergency bylaws or the resolution approving the list are met` `the period of time has not run beyond what is reasonably necessary after the termination of the emergency` `the deeming is required to provide a quorum at the meeting of the board of directors` MEANS
        `the person is an officer or other person designated on a list approved by the board of directors before the emergency`
    AND `the person's turn in the order of priority has come and the conditions provided in the emergency bylaws or the resolution approving the list are met`
    AND `the period of time has not run beyond what is reasonably necessary after the termination of the emergency`
    AND `the deeming is required to provide a quorum at the meeting of the board of directors`

§§ `s 110(b) to (h) Succession, offices, liability, notice, officers as directors`

-- src:150 | (b) The board of directors, either before or during any such emergency, may provide, and from time to time modify, lines of succession in the event that during such emergency any or all officers or agents of the corporation shall for any reason be rendered incapable of discharging their duties.
