@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(b), (c) (src:150-151)
DECLARE `s 110(b) Time of the board's action` IS ONE OF
    `before the emergency`
    `during the emergency`
    `after the emergency`

-- Lines of succession, and the head office: the board may act "either before or during any such emergency". An act
-- after the emergency is not covered by the subsection (NOTHING).
-- src:150 | (b) The board of directors, either before or during any such emergency, may provide, and from time to time modify, lines of succession in the event that during such emergency any or all officers or agents of the corporation shall for any reason be rendered incapable of discharging their duties.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(b) (src:150)
GIVEN time IS A `s 110(b) Time of the board's action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(b) the board of directors may provide, and from time to time modify, lines of succession` time MEANS
    CONSIDER time
    WHEN `before the emergency` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `during the emergency` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `after the emergency` THEN NOTHING

-- src:151 | (c) The board of directors, either before or during any such emergency, may, effective in the emergency, change the head office or designate several alternative head offices or regional offices, or authorize the officers so to do.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(c) (src:151)
GIVEN time IS A `s 110(b) Time of the board's action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(c) the board of directors may, effective in the emergency, change the head office or designate alternative head offices or regional offices, or authorize the officers to do so` time MEANS
    CONSIDER time
    WHEN `before the emergency` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `during the emergency` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `after the emergency` THEN NOTHING

-- No officer, director or employee acting in accordance with any emergency bylaws is liable except for wilful
-- misconduct. The rule says whether the protection applies; liability for wilful misconduct is a matter for other
-- law. Any other kind of person is not covered (NOTHING).
-- src:152 | (d) No officer, director or employee acting in accordance with any emergency bylaws shall be liable except for wilful misconduct.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(d) (src:152)
GIVEN person IS AN Actor
      `the person is acting in accordance with the emergency bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's conduct is wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(d) the person is protected from liability` person `the person is acting in accordance with the emergency bylaws` `the person's conduct is wilful misconduct` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `an officer` THEN JUST (`the person is acting in accordance with the emergency bylaws` AND (NOT (`the person's conduct is wilful misconduct`)))
    WHEN `a director` THEN JUST (`the person is acting in accordance with the emergency bylaws` AND (NOT (`the person's conduct is wilful misconduct`)))
    WHEN `an employee` THEN JUST (`the person is acting in accordance with the emergency bylaws` AND (NOT (`the person's conduct is wilful misconduct`)))
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Notice of a board meeting during an emergency, unless otherwise provided in emergency bylaws, may be given only to
-- such of the directors as it may be feasible to reach at the time and by such means as may be feasible at the time,
-- including publication or radio. If the emergency bylaws provide otherwise they govern (NOTHING).
-- src:154 | (f) Unless otherwise provided in emergency bylaws, notice of any meeting of the board of directors during such an emergency may be given only to such of the directors as it may be feasible to reach at the time and by such means as may be feasible at the time, including publication or radio.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(f) (src:154)
GIVEN `the emergency bylaws provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given to every director it was feasible to reach at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was given by means that were feasible at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 110(f) the notice of the meeting of the board of directors is sufficient` `the emergency bylaws provide otherwise` `the notice was given to every director it was feasible to reach at the time` `the notice was given by means that were feasible at the time` MEANS
    IF `the emergency bylaws provide otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the notice was given to every director it was feasible to reach at the time` AND `the notice was given by means that were feasible at the time`)

-- To the extent required to constitute a quorum at a board meeting during the emergency, the officers who are
-- present are, unless the emergency bylaws provide otherwise, deemed directors for the meeting, in order of rank and,
-- within the same rank, in order of seniority. The officer's place is counted from 1.
-- src:155 | (g) To the extent required to constitute a quorum at any meeting of the board of directors during such an emergency, the officers of the corporation who are present shall, unless otherwise provided in emergency bylaws, be deemed, in order of rank and within the same rank in order of seniority, directors for such meeting.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(g) (src:155)
GIVEN `the emergency bylaws provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer's place among the officers present in order of rank and, within the same rank, seniority` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of directors lacking to constitute a quorum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(g) the officer present is deemed a director for the meeting` `the emergency bylaws provide otherwise` `the officer's place among the officers present in order of rank and, within the same rank, seniority` `the number of directors lacking to constitute a quorum` MEANS
        (NOT (`the emergency bylaws provide otherwise`))
    AND (`the officer's place among the officers present in order of rank and, within the same rank, seniority` AT LEAST 1)
    AND (`the officer's place among the officers present in order of rank and, within the same rank, seniority` AT MOST `the number of directors lacking to constitute a quorum`)

-- Nothing in the section is exclusive of other provisions for emergency powers consistent with other sections of
-- this title that have been or may be adopted.
