@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(h) (src:156)
GIVEN `the provision for emergency powers is consistent with other sections of this title` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(h) the provision for emergency powers is permitted in addition to this section` `the provision for emergency powers is consistent with other sections of this title` MEANS
    `the provision for emergency powers is consistent with other sections of this title`

§§ `s 110(i) An emergency condition: meetings of stockholders and dividends`

-- During any emergency condition of a type described in subsection (a), the board (or, if a quorum cannot be readily
-- convened for a meeting, a majority of the directors present) may take any action that it determines to be practical
-- and necessary to address the circumstances with respect to a meeting of stockholders, notwithstanding anything to the
-- contrary in the chapter, in Chapter 7 of Title 5 or in the certificate or bylaws, including to postpone a meeting to a
-- later time or date.
-- src:157 | (i) During any emergency condition of a type described in subsection (a) of this section, the board of directors (or, if a quorum cannot be readily convened for a meeting, a majority of the directors present) may (i) take any action that it determines to be practical and necessary to address the circumstances of such emergency condition with respect to a meeting of stockholders of the corporation notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this chapter or in Chapter 7 of Title 5 or in the certificate of incorporation or bylaws, including, but not limited to, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 110(i) (src:157)
GIVEN emergency IS A `s 110(a) Emergency`
      `a quorum of the board of directors can readily be convened for a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board of directors acted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a majority of the directors present acted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 110(i) the action with respect to the meeting of stockholders is authorized` emergency `a quorum of the board of directors can readily be convened for a meeting` `the board of directors acted` `a majority of the directors present acted` MEANS
        (NOT (emergency EQUALS `no emergency`))
    AND (IF `a quorum of the board of directors can readily be convened for a meeting`
         THEN `the board of directors acted`
         ELSE (`the board of directors acted` OR `a majority of the directors present acted`))

