        (NOT (emergency EQUALS `no emergency`))
    AND `it was not practicable to allow inspection of the stocklist during the emergency condition`

§ `Section 112 -- Access to proxy solicitation materials`

-- The bylaws may provide that if the corporation solicits proxies with respect to an election of directors, it may be
-- required to include in its proxy solicitation materials (including any form of proxy), in addition to individuals
-- nominated by the board, 1 or more individuals nominated by a stockholder, subject to the procedures or conditions
-- the bylaws provide.
-- src:176 | The bylaws may provide that if the corporation solicits proxies with respect to an election of directors, it may be required, to the extent and subject to such procedures or conditions as may be provided in the bylaws, to include in its proxy solicitation materials (including any form of proxy it distributes), in addition to individuals nominated by …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 112 (src:176)
GIVEN `the bylaws so provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation solicits proxies with respect to an election of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has met the procedures and conditions the bylaws provide` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 112 the corporation may be required to include the stockholder's nominee in its proxy solicitation materials` `the bylaws so provide` `the corporation solicits proxies with respect to an election of directors` `the stockholder has met the procedures and conditions the bylaws provide` MEANS
        `the bylaws so provide`
    AND `the corporation solicits proxies with respect to an election of directors`
    AND `the stockholder has met the procedures and conditions the bylaws provide`

-- src:176 | the board of directors, 1 or more individuals nominated by a stockholder. Such procedures or conditions may include any of the following:
-- src:177 | (1) A provision requiring a minimum record or beneficial ownership, or duration of ownership, of shares of the corporation’s capital stock, by the nominating stockholder, and defining beneficial ownership to take into account options or other rights in respect of or related to such stock;
-- src:178 | (2) A provision requiring the nominating stockholder to submit specified information concerning the stockholder and the stockholder’s nominees, including information concerning ownership by such persons of shares of the corporation’s capital stock, or options or other rights in respect of or related to such stock;
-- src:179 | (3) A provision conditioning eligibility to require inclusion in the corporation’s proxy solicitation materials upon the number or proportion of directors nominated by stockholders or whether the stockholder previously sought to require such inclusion;
-- src:180 | (4) A provision precluding nominations by any person if such person, any nominee of such person, or any affiliate or associate of such person or nominee, has acquired or publicly proposed to acquire shares constituting a specified percentage of the voting power of the corporation’s outstanding voting stock within a specified period before the election of directors;
-- src:181 | (5) A provision requiring that the nominating stockholder undertake to indemnify the corporation in respect of any loss arising as a result of any false or misleading information or statement submitted by the nominating stockholder in connection with a nomination; and
-- src:182 | (6) Any other lawful condition.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 112 (src:176-182)
DECLARE `s 112 Condition of access` IS ONE OF
    `a minimum record or beneficial ownership, or duration of ownership, of shares of the corporation's capital stock by the nominating stockholder`
    `submission of specified information concerning the stockholder and the stockholder's nominees`
    `eligibility conditioned upon the number or proportion of directors nominated by stockholders or whether the stockholder previously sought to require such inclusion`
    `preclusion of nominations by a person, a nominee or an affiliate or associate who has acquired or publicly proposed to acquire a specified percentage of the voting power within a specified period before the election`
    `the nominating stockholder's undertaking to indemnify the corporation in respect of any loss arising from false or misleading information`
    `any other condition`

-- src:176 | the board of directors, 1 or more individuals nominated by a stockholder. Such procedures or conditions may include any of the following:
-- src:182 | (6) Any other lawful condition.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 112 (src:176-182)
GIVEN condition IS A `s 112 Condition of access`
      `the condition is lawful` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 112 the bylaws may impose the condition` condition `the condition is lawful` MEANS
    CONSIDER condition
    WHEN `a minimum record or beneficial ownership, or duration of ownership, of shares of the corporation's capital stock by the nominating stockholder` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `submission of specified information concerning the stockholder and the stockholder's nominees` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `eligibility conditioned upon the number or proportion of directors nominated by stockholders or whether the stockholder previously sought to require such inclusion` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `preclusion of nominations by a person, a nominee or an affiliate or associate who has acquired or publicly proposed to acquire a specified percentage of the voting power within a specified period before the election` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the nominating stockholder's undertaking to indemnify the corporation in respect of any loss arising from false or misleading information` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other condition` THEN `the condition is lawful`

§ `Section 113 -- Proxy expense reimbursement`

-- The bylaws may provide for the reimbursement by the corporation of expenses incurred by a stockholder in soliciting
-- proxies in connection with an election of directors, subject to the procedures or conditions the bylaws prescribe.
-- No bylaw so adopted applies to elections for which any record date precedes its adoption: a bylaw adopted on the
-- record date itself is not preceded by it, so it applies.
-- src:186 | (a) The bylaws may provide for the reimbursement by the corporation of expenses incurred by a stockholder in soliciting proxies in connection with an election of directors, subject to such procedures or conditions as the bylaws may prescribe, …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 113(a) (src:186)
GIVEN `the bylaws so provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expenses were incurred by the stockholder in soliciting proxies in connection with an election of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the stockholder has met the procedures and conditions the bylaws prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 113(a) the corporation may be required to reimburse the stockholder's expenses` `the bylaws so provide` `the expenses were incurred by the stockholder in soliciting proxies in connection with an election of directors` `the stockholder has met the procedures and conditions the bylaws prescribe` MEANS
        `the bylaws so provide`
    AND `the expenses were incurred by the stockholder in soliciting proxies in connection with an election of directors`
    AND `the stockholder has met the procedures and conditions the bylaws prescribe`

-- src:186 | (a) The bylaws may provide for the reimbursement by the corporation of expenses incurred by a stockholder in soliciting proxies in connection with an election of directors, subject to such procedures or conditions as the bylaws may prescribe, …
-- src:187 | (1) Conditioning eligibility for reimbursement upon the number or proportion of persons nominated by the stockholder seeking reimbursement or whether such stockholder previously sought reimbursement for similar expenses;
-- src:188 | (2) Limitations on the amount of reimbursement based upon the proportion of votes cast in favor of 1 or more of the persons nominated by the stockholder seeking reimbursement, or upon the amount spent by the corporation in soliciting proxies in connection with the election;
-- src:189 | (3) Limitations concerning elections of directors by cumulative voting pursuant to § 214 of this title; or
-- src:190 | (4) Any other lawful condition.
